// expect: 28
// The interval fragment's acceptance face: the lower-bound read
// discharges what the ground fold alone cannot — `cap` through the
// if-join + the len floor, `bump` through Add over the opaque-face type
// read of its refined param. `wild` is the SOUNDNESS control: before
// the value_flows_class licence its `v - 1` was laundered through the
// arith class (a runtime -1 escaped a `0 <= self` return, measured);
// now it pends visibly and still runs (debt surfaces, never blocks).
// `wrap` proves the CALLEE leg: an authored return rides the
// pre-registered TFun as a Ty VALUE, so a call's bound reads the
// callee's own annotation verbatim — uncontaminatable by class
// merging. `seek` is the named self-call residue: the recursion's IH
// needs the decl-class discriminator (a self-call's callee cell shares
// the decl's union-find class; a tail-called OTHER fn must never be
// granted the IH — the g-launder), so it pends honestly until
// graph_root_of lands. The frontier leg asserts exactly TWO pending
// comparisons survive this file (seek + wild), no more (the engine
// discharges), no fewer (the licence never launders).
type Nat = Int where 0 <= self

fn cap(xs) -> Nat = if len(xs) < 16 { 16 } else { len(xs) }

fn bump(v: Nat) -> Nat = v + 1

fn base() -> Nat = 7

fn wrap() -> Nat = base()

fn seek(xs, i: Nat) -> Nat = if i >= len(xs) { 0 } else { seek(xs, i + 1) }

fn wild(v: Nat) -> Nat = v - 1

fn main() = bump(cap([1, 2, 3])) + seek([1, 2, 3], 0) + wild(5) + wrap()
